      "i18n": {
        "en": {
          "title": "Human papillomavirus (HPV) vaccine",
          "summary": "Government-funded HPV vaccine is offered to first-year junior high students (boys included from the 2025 school year): two doses 6 months apart at school, protecting against cervical and other HPV-related cancers.",
          "bodyMarkdown": "HPV infection is linked to cervical, anal and oropharyngeal cancers. Vaccination works best before sexual activity begins.\n\nThe government-funded programme covers **first-year junior high school students**, mainly at school: two doses 6 months apart; students who miss school sessions can catch up at contracted clinics. Others can pay for vaccination; those starting at 15 or older need 3 doses."
        }
      },
